One thing I'd change from our previous approach

I wouldn't immediately call this Phase 1.9.1 implementation.

First, let's do:

PHASE 1.9 — PRE-IMPLEMENTATION ARCHITECTURAL AUDIT

Read-only.

Exactly like we did for Phase 1.8:

NO production changes
NO test changes
NO migrations
NO dependency additions
NO implementation


Only inspect → reason → document → identify decisions.

Then we can let Antigravity produce the architectural report.

If it's GREEN, we lock the implementation specification and start Phase 1.9.1.

If it's YELLOW, we resolve the decisions first.

If it's RED, we stop and redesign.

That's the safest way to build this. 🧱☁️

And yes — from this point forward, I'd keep using this phase → audit → implementation → post-audit → commit rhythm for the Backup & Restore system.